   "title": "Ododo Renames Kogi Specialist Hospital After Ex-Gov Ibrahim Idris",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/ododo-renames-kogi-specialist-hospital-after-ex-gov-ibrahim-idris/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:57:24 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793350644.0,
   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "He described Ibrahim Idris as a distinguished statesman whose leadership and service had left an enduring mark on the state. “Therefore, as the Chief Servant of Kogi State, I am pleased to announce that the Kogi State Specialist Hospital in Lokoja will henceforth be renamed Ibrahim Idris Specialist Hospital, Lokoja, in honour of this distinguished former governor and in recognition of his contributions to the development of our dear state,” Ododo said.",
   "summary_zh": "他称易卜拉欣·伊德里斯是一位杰出的政治家，其领导能力和奉献精神在州内留下了长久印记。奥多多说：“因此，作为科吉州首席仆人，我很高兴宣布，位于洛科贾的科吉州专科医院今后将更名为‘易卜拉欣·伊德里斯专科医院’，以纪念这位杰出的前州长，并认可他为我们亲爱的州所作的发展贡献。”",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Ododo announced the decision yesterday during the 40th-day prayer for the repose of the former governor’s soul in Abejukolo, Omala local government area of the state. The governor said the gesture was in recognition of the late leader’s contributions to the development of Kogi State, noting that his legacy deserved to be preserved for present and future generations. He described Ibrahim Idris as a distinguished statesman whose leadership and service had left an enduring mark on the state. “Therefore, as the Chief Servant of Kogi State, I am pleased to announce that the Kogi State Specialist Hospital in Lokoja will henceforth be renamed Ibrahim Idris Specialist Hospital, Lokoja, in honour of this distinguished former governor and in recognition of his contributions to the development of our dear state,” Ododo said. The governor said his administration remained committed to recognising leaders who had contributed to the growth and development of the state, adding that their achievements should continue to inspire future generations. Ododo also called on the people of Kogi State to embrace unity and rise above political, ethnic and religious differences. He said the presence of people from diverse political backgrounds, ethnic groups and religious persuasions at the prayer was a testament to the late governor’s ability to build bridges and foster relationships across different divides. According to him, unity remains essential for the collective progress of the state, while division weakens communities and undermines development. Earlier, the Chairman of the Organising Committee for the 40th-day prayer, Alhaji Musa Amodu, commended Ododo for his support towards the burial arrangements and the prayer programme. Amodu disclosed that the governor had continued to support the family following the former governor’s death, including providing financial assistance for the burial and fully sponsoring the 40th-day prayer. Ibrahim Idris governed Kogi State from May 29, 2003, to January 2012 on the platform of the Peoples Democratic Party (PDP). He secured a second term following the March 2008 governorship re-run election and remained influential in the state’s political and business circles after leaving office. He died in the United Kingdom on September 20, 2026, at the age of 77, following an illness, and was buried on September 25, 2026, at Gudu Cemetery in Apo, Abuja. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol",
    "eco"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_leadership",
   "title_zh": "奥多多将科吉专科医院更名为前州长易卜拉欣·伊德里斯医院",
   "body_zh": "奥多多昨日在该州奥马拉地方政府区域阿贝朱科洛举行前州长逝世40天祈祷仪式期间宣布了这一决定。州长表示，此举是为认可已故领导人对科吉州发展的贡献，并指出他的精神遗产值得当代及子孙后代传承。他称易卜拉欣·伊德里斯是一位杰出的政治家，其领导和服务给该州留下了持久印记。奥多多说：“因此，作为科吉州的首席仆人，我很高兴宣布，位于洛科贾的科吉州专科医院今后将更名为洛科贾易卜拉欣·伊德里斯专科医院，以纪念这位杰出的前州长，并认可他对我们挚爱州发展的贡献。”州长表示，其政府仍致力于表彰那些为该州成长和发展作出贡献的领导人，并补充说，他们的成就应继续激励后代。奥多多还呼吁科吉州人民拥抱团结，超越政治、族群和宗教差异。他说，不同政治背景、族群和宗教信仰的人士出席祈祷仪式，证明已故州长有能力弥合分歧、建立跨越不同界限的联系。他认为，团结仍是全州共同进步的关键，而分裂会削弱社区并阻碍发展。此前，第40天祈祷仪式组织委员会主席阿哈吉·穆萨·阿莫杜称赞奥多多为安葬筹备工作和祈祷活动提供的支持。阿莫杜透露，前州长去世后，州长一直继续支持其家属，包括为安葬提供经济援助，并全额赞助第40天祈祷仪式。易卜拉欣·伊德里斯于2003年5月29日至2012年1月以人民民主党（PDP）的名义执政科吉州。他在2008年3月州长选举重跑后赢得第二个任期，离任后仍在该州政治和商业圈颇具影响力。他因病于2026年9月20日在英国去世，享年77岁，并于2026年9月25日安葬在阿布贾阿波的古杜公墓。掌握最新动态。获取实时报道、独家内幕和独家视角，直接发送到您的手机。不要满足于过时新闻。加入LEADERSHIP NEWS的WhatsApp，随时随地接收24/7最新消息 →",
