   "title": "Swiss foreign minister visits N. Korea amid opening of 1st diplomatic office",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/foreignaffairs/northkorea/20261030/swiss-foreign-minister-visits-n-korea-amid-opening-of-1st-diplomatic-office",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:57:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793350623.0,
   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "Cassis has arrived in North Korea, Pyongyang's state media reported Friday, as Switzerland has opened its first diplomatic office in the North. The Swiss government earlier said Cassis will visit North Korea on a two-day trip from Thursday to attend the official reopening of the Swiss diplomatic office in Pyongyang and hold political talks with North Korean officials.",
   "summary_zh": "朝鲜国家媒体报道称，卡西斯已抵达朝鲜。瑞士在朝鲜开设了首个外交办事处。此前，瑞士政府表示，卡西斯将于周四起对朝鲜进行为期两天的访问，出席瑞士驻平壤外交办事处正式重新开放仪式，并与朝鲜官员举行政治会谈。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Swiss Foreign Minister Ignazio Cassis has arrived in North Korea, Pyongyang's state media reported Friday, as Switzerland has opened its first diplomatic office in the North. Cassis arrived in Pyongyang the previous day, greeted by North Korean foreign ministry officials, the North's ambassador to Switzerland and others at the airport, according to the Korean Central News Agency (KCNA). The KCNA did not elaborate on other details, such as the purpose of his visit and itinerary. The Swiss government earlier said Cassis will visit North Korea on a two-day trip from Thursday to attend the official reopening of the Swiss diplomatic office in Pyongyang and hold political talks with North Korean officials. The establishment of the diplomatic office marks Switzerland's first political and diplomatic installations in Pyongyang since the two countries forged diplomatic relations in 1974. \"Against a backdrop of heightened tensions and limited international contact, Switzerland intends to continue its commitment in the region,\" the Swiss government said in a release. \"Through its presence in Pyongyang, it aims to maintain direct dialogue, including on matters of disagreement. Switzerland opened an office on humanitarian cooperation in Pyongyang in 1997, but it closed down in 2020 due to the COVID-19 pandemic lockdown",
