   "title": "2027: Onaiyekan backs opposition’s unity push against Tinubu",
   "url": "https://www.vanguardngr.com/2026/10/2027-onaiyekan-backs-oppositions-unity-push-against-tinubu/",
   "domain": "vanguardngr.com",
   "source": "vanguardngr.com",
   "published": "Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:56:49 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793350609.0,
   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "Roman Catholic Cardinal John Onaiyekan has thrown his weight behind efforts by opposition parties under the G100 Coalition to present a united front ahead of the 2027 elections, as the Coalition prepares to hold its second summit on Monday, November 9, 2026. The Cardinal expressed support for the efforts of opposition parties and their candidates to unite, with the aim of building “a robust opposition which is vital to the sustenance of Nigeria’s democratic traditions”.",
   "summary_zh": "在G100联盟准备于2026年11月9日星期一举行第二次峰会之际，罗马天主教枢机主教约翰·奥奈耶坎支持反对党组成统一阵线，为2027年选举做准备。枢机主教表示，支持反对党及其候选人团结一致，以打造“强大的反对力量，这对维系尼日利亚的民主传统至关重要”。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Roman Catholic Cardinal John Onaiyekan has thrown his weight behind efforts by opposition parties under the G100 Coalition to present a united front ahead of the 2027 elections, as the Coalition prepares to hold its second summit on Monday, November 9, 2026. The leaders of the Coalition, comprising National Chairmen and National Secretaries of some political parties, briefed the Cardinal at his residence on Thursday in Abuja. In a statement signed on behalf of the Coalition Parties, Salihu Moh. Lukman said the leaders told His Eminence about “initiatives and efforts being made to present a united front of opposition political parties and ensure that Nigerians are presented with a credible alternative to rescue the country.” Among those who met the cardinal were the factional national chairman of the Peoples Democratic Party (PDP), Alhaji Kabiru Tanimu Turaki SAN, and the faction’s national secretary, Honourable Daniel Woyengikuro. The Social Democratic Party SDP National Chairman, Professor Sadiq Umar Abubakar Gombe, and the People’s Redemption Party PRP National Chairman, Dr Hakeem Baba Ahmed, were also there, alongside the PRP National Secretary, Mr Sunny Kanu. Professor Jibrin Ibrahim, a civil society activist and scholar, facilitated the meeting. According to the statement, Coalition leaders are working to conclude and adopt the papers before the Second Summit on November 9, where all the political parties under the Coalition will endorse and unveil them. The Cardinal expressed support for the efforts of opposition parties and their candidates to unite, with the aim of building “a robust opposition which is vital to the sustenance of Nigeria’s democratic traditions”. It also thanked the Cardinal for his “lifelong stand for justice and compassion” and asked him to continue to pray for the success of the Coalition. The statement added that the Coalition leaders will visit other distinguished Nigerians and diplomatic missions in the coming weeks. It said the Coalition is focused on giving the country and its citizens “greater faith and capacities in solving our problems with new leadership, new vision and new focus on rebuilding citizens’ welfare, security and trust in leadership. Comments expressed here do not reflect the opinions of Vanguard newspapers or any employee thereof",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
