   "title": "Tinubu Departs Abuja for Makkah Thursday to Pray for Nigeria, Presidency Announces",
   "url": "https://www.thisdaylive.com/2026/10/28/tinubu-departs-abuja-for-makkah-thursday-to-pray-for-nigeria-presidency-announces/",
   "domain": "thisdaylive.com",
   "source": "ThisDay（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:15:07 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793218507.0,
   "ageDays": 1.56,
   "summary": "President Bola Ahmed Tinubu will depart Abuja on Thursday for Makkah, Saudi Arabia, to perform Umrah, an Islamic spiritual exercise involving a pilgrimage to the Holy City. According to a statement issued on Wednesday by Bayo Onanuga, Special Adviser to the President on Information and Strategy, the visit will provide Tinubu an opportunity for spiritual reflection, devotion and prayers for Nigeria.",
   "summary_zh": "博拉·艾哈迈德·蒂努布总统将于周四离开阿布贾，前往沙特阿拉伯麦加perform Umrah。这是一种需要前往圣城朝觐的伊斯兰宗教活动。总统信息与战略特别顾问Bayo Onanuga于周三发表声明称，此次访问将为蒂努布提供机会进行精神反思、宗教敬奉并为尼日利亚祈祷。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "President Bola Ahmed Tinubu will depart Abuja on Thursday for Makkah, Saudi Arabia, to perform Umrah, an Islamic spiritual exercise involving a pilgrimage to the Holy City. According to a statement issued on Wednesday by Bayo Onanuga, Special Adviser to the President on Information and Strategy, the visit will provide Tinubu an opportunity for spiritual reflection, devotion and prayers for Nigeria. “The visit gives the President an opportunity for spiritual reflection, devotion, and prayers for Nigeria’s peace, unity, stability, and continued progress,” the statement said. Onanuga said the President would perform the religious rites associated with Umrah while seeking divine guidance and blessings for the country and its people. “While in Makkah, President Tinubu will perform the religious rites associated with Umrah, seeking Allah’s guidance and blessings for Nigeria and its people,” the statement added. Before departing Abuja, the President is expected to commission equipment acquired by the Nigerian Air Force for its operations. The commissioning will take place at the Presidential Wing of the Nnamdi Azikiwe International Airport. Tinubu is expected to return to Nigeria next week after completing the spiritual exercise. Founded on January 22, 1995, THISDAY is published by THISDAY NEWSPAPERS LTD., 35 Creek Road Apapa, Lagos, Nigeria with offices in 36 states of Nigeria , the Federal Capital Territory and around the world. It is Nigeria’s most authoritative news media available on all platforms for the political, business, professional and diplomatic elite and broader middle classes while serving as the meeting point of new ideas, culture and technology for the aspirationals and millennials. The newspaper is a public trust dedicated to the pursuit of truth and reason covering a range of issues from breaking news to politics, business, the markets, the arts, sports and community to the crossroads of people and society. You can email us at: hello@thisdaylive.com or visit our contact us page",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
